+- A tool's images reach the model on every translation (`toolOutput` in [`ir.go`](../../internal/gateway/ir.go) reads them from Anthropic's `tool_result`, Responses' `function_call_output`, such as Codex's `view_image` output `[{"type":"input_image","image_url":"data:…"}]`, and a Chat tool message). Anthropic's Messages keeps them in the `tool_result`. Chat, Qoder and Cursor (`cursorImage`) put them in a user message right after the results, and the result says they follow. Command Code puts them in the user's turn after the results, Gemini and Code Assist after the function's response, and Devin in its tool message. Kiro's results hold text alone, so Kiro (the built-in, and its plugin from 0.1.9 on) sends them with the message that answers the call, and only the latest images go again (#369, #1861). `TestCodexToolImageReachesAnthropicPlugin`, `TestCodexToolImageKiro`, `TestCodexToolImageCursor`, and the plugin's `tool-images.test.mjs`.- Group members are `provider/model[:effort]`. A member with a fixed effort is asked for that effort, bounded by the group's levels (#671).
 - A group offers agents the reasoning levels its members have in common (`groupEntries` in [`group.go`](../../internal/provider/group.go)), or the ones it names (`Group.Levels`, #295). A member that doesn't follow the agent's effort is left out of that: one fixed at an effort, one whose levels nothing knows (#597), one that thinks with no levels, one the user made reasonless, and one known not to think (`Entry.Quiet`), which the gateway sends no reasoning ask (`withoutReasoningAsk`, [`quiet.go`](../../internal/gateway/quiet.go)). A quiet member used to empty the group's levels, so Codex got its entry with no `supported_reasoning_levels`, showed no effort control and ran at its own medium (#2127, `TestGroupQuietMemberKeepsCodexEffortControl`).
 - An agent whose config can't carry an effort has one picked in magpie (`provider.AgentEffort`, settings' `agentEfforts`; Cursor Private Inference's row, #1003). It is asked for on that agent's requests to a model that reasons (`Provider.Thinks`), in place of the level the request sent, fitted to the model's levels and bounded by the group's. Order: a member's fixed effort, then a model's `:effort` suffix, then the turn's pick (a routing rule's), then the agent's pick, then the request's own. A model that doesn't reason is sent as asked; the default (none picked) leaves every request as it came. The pick beats the request's own because Cursor sends its own default as often as a real choice. Picking Default hands the choice back to Cursor.
 - In models.dev, entries from `deepseek`, `kimi-code-plan-cn` and `kimi-code-plan-global` gain `none` only when they have both a `toggle` and effort levels; the DeepSeek and Kimi APIs accepted that value in [#1098](https://github.com/yetone/magpie/issues/1098). Other providers keep their listed levels because their APIs may reject `none`; toggle-only entries remain level-less ([`mdModel.efforts`](../../internal/catalog/catalog.go)).
